The legal texts come from official publications of the Republic of Côte d'Ivoire:

  Assemblée nationale de Côte d'Ivoire, Loi n° 2016-886 du 08 novembre 2016 portant Constitution de la
  République de Côte d'Ivoire,
  https://www.assnat.ci/IMG/pdf/constitution_de_la_republique_de_cote_d_ivoireloi_-_no_2016-886_du_08_novembre_2016.pdf,
  retrieved 28 October 2026;
  WIPO Lex (World Intellectual Property Organization), record CI023, Loi n° 2016-886 du 08 novembre 2016 portant
  constitution de la République de Côte d'Ivoire, telle que modifiée par la loi constitutionnelle n° 2020-348 du
  19 mars 2020, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/fr/legislation/details/22491, retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Assemblée nationale's site reads "Copyright ©2019 assnat.ci - Tous droits resevés" and publishes no licence for
the legal texts; WIPO Lex reproduces national legislation for information under WIPO's general terms of use. They
are official legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the
attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, apostrophes, quotes and list dashes were normalised; page numbers, headings, the promulgation formula and
the signature lines were removed; and the text was arranged as git commits credited to the laws concerned. The
wording of the law was not changed, except where REPRODUCE.md lists a transcription slip in WIPO's copy and the 2016
wording was kept. None of the publishers endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
